@page
@model HrSystemDhg.Web.Pages.Admin.AutomationModel
@{ViewData["Title"]="Automation & n8n";}
<div class="eyebrow">CONNECTED WORKFLOWS</div><h1>Automation &amp; n8n</h1>
<p>Connect tasks, meetings, attendance and payroll to your own n8n workflows. Calculations, permissions and approvals remain in Garowe City.</p>
@if(TempData["AutomationNotice"] is string notice){<p class="notice" role="status">@notice</p>}
<div asp-validation-summary="All"></div>
<nav class="workspace-tabs"><a href="#automation-settings">Connection</a><a href="#automation-workflows">Workflows &amp; read-only API</a><a href="#automation-history">Delivery history</a></nav>
<section class="card" id="automation-settings"><h2>Connection settings</h2><p>Delivery is off until you configure a production webhook and enable it. Use your n8n workflow’s Production URL, not the editor or assistant address.</p>
<form method="post"><label>Production webhook URL<input asp-for="Input.WebhookUrl" type="url" placeholder="https://your-instance.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/garowe-city-events" maxlength="2048" /></label>
<label>Webhook shared password<input asp-for="WebhookPassword" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" maxlength="512" placeholder="@(Model.HasWebhookPassword?"Configured — leave blank to keep":"Choose 16–512 characters")" /></label><p>In n8n, select Header Auth with header name <code>X-Garowe-Webhook-Key</code> and the same password. The saved value is encrypted and never displayed.</p>
<fieldset><legend>Module events</legend><div class="grid"><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.Tasks"/> Task creation, assignment and progress</label><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.Meetings"/> Meeting creation, updates, attendance and published minutes</label><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.Attendance"/> Device punches and calculated attendance</label><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.Payroll"/> Payroll stages and payslip publication</label></div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Scheduled notifications</legend><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.AllowReminders"/> Allow n8n to queue preset in-app task/meeting reminders and daily admin digests</label><p>A separate limited key is required. Jobs recheck current records and permissions and use duplicate protection. They cannot change tasks, approve payroll or adjust attendance.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Optional read-only data sharing</legend><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.IncludeContacts"/> Allow lookup of registered email and WhatsApp numbers for event recipients</label><label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.IncludePayrollAmounts"/> Include aggregate gross/net totals in payroll summaries</label><p>These are off by default. Events exclude passwords, biometric templates, bank details and individual salary amounts. Approved leave is explicitly marked in attendance summaries.</p></fieldset>
<label class="inline"><input asp-for="Input.Enabled"/> Enable event delivery and the read-only automation API</label><button>Save automation settings</button></form>
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Test"><button class="secondary">Send test event</button><p>The test contains no employee data. A delivered status means n8n acknowledged the webhook; it does not confirm downstream WhatsApp or email delivery.</p></form></section>
<section class="card" id="automation-workflows"><h2>Workflows &amp; read-only API</h2><p>Import these templates into n8n, configure its credentials and connect the final action nodes to your chosen notification or reporting service before publishing. They start inactive. Reminder and daily jobs queue in-app notifications after you enable reminder access and publish their schedules. Event receiver branches can be extended with optional WhatsApp/email actions.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" asp-page-handler="Workflow" asp-route-kind="events">Download event receiver</a><a class="button secondary" asp-page-handler="Workflow" asp-route-kind="reminders">Download reminder schedule</a><a class="button secondary" asp-page-handler="Workflow" asp-route-kind="daily">Download daily notifications</a><a class="button secondary" asp-page-handler="Workflow" asp-route-kind="reports">Download report-data readers</a></div>
<p>Schedules use <strong>Africa/Mogadishu</strong>. Daily reports run at 4 PM Saturday–Thursday; reminder checks run every 15 minutes. Use event IDs/reminder keys to prevent duplicate notifications, and choose either existing WhatsApp delivery or n8n for each message type.</p>
<p>Read-only summaries: <code>/api/integrations/n8n/summary?module=tasks</code> (also meetings, attendance, payroll). Recipients: <code>/api/integrations/n8n/recipients?eventId=EVENT_ID</code>. Both require <code>X-Garowe-Automation-Key</code>, and only enabled modules are accessible.</p>
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Rotate"><button class="secondary">@(Model.HasCallbackKey?"Rotate / download read-only key":"Generate / download read-only key")</button><p>Store the downloaded key in an n8n Header Auth credential. Rotating immediately revokes the previous key. It cannot change records, approve payroll or waive deductions.</p></form><form method="post" asp-page-handler="ReminderKey"><button class="secondary">Generate / rotate reminder-job key</button><p>Store this separate key in n8n as header <code>X-Garowe-Reminder-Key</code>. It can queue only the preset in-app reminders/digests when explicitly enabled. WhatsApp/email actions require their own provider setup.</p></form></section>
<section class="card table-scroll" id="automation-history"><h2>Delivery history</h2><p>Latest 100 events. Retries use the same event ID, with up to eight automatic attempts. Disabling delivery pauses queued events; changing the destination cancels events for the previous destination.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Created (UTC)</th><th>Module / event</th><th>Status</th><th>Attempts</th><th>HTTP</th><th>Details</th><th>Actions</th></tr></thead><tbody>@foreach(var row in Model.Deliveries){<tr><td>@row.CreatedUtc.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss")</td><td>@row.Module<br/>@row.EventType</td><td><span class="badge">@row.Status</span></td><td>@row.Attempts</td><td>@row.LastHttpStatus</td><td>@row.LastError<small>@row.Id</small></td><td>@if(row.Status=="Failed"){<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Retry"><input type="hidden" name="id" value="@row.Id"/><button class="secondary">Retry</button></form>}@if(row.Status is "Pending" or "Retrying" or "Failed"){<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Cancel"><input type="hidden" name="id" value="@row.Id"/><button class="secondary">Cancel delivery</button></form>}</td></tr>}</tbody></table></section>
